## Current decision to resolve

Compare the durable Original and Automatic captures and answer one question:

> Can the Automatic candidate be accepted as a recognizable, source-only
> temporal simplification for this phrase while preserving every reviewed
> `M`/`H` event and without adding new pitches?

Record exactly one outcome:

- `accept-source-reduction`: the reviewed IDs and listening notes support the
  candidate; record any dropped `D` IDs and keep the source fingerprint.
- `retain-source-reduction-partial`: the candidate is useful as an engineering
  preview but not yet musically accepted; keep Original as the default and
  record the failing identity/rhythm/comfort reason.
- `reject-and-review`: the candidate changes a reviewed identity event or is
  audibly/physically unacceptable; record the smallest offending source-ID
  set.

The listener can complete this decision now, before any new source annotation.
The four required musical notes are: recognizability, backing usefulness,
melody audibility, and hand comfort with normal sustain. They are acceptance
ratings, not claims inferred from hashes, event counts, or waveform duration.
